\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {I}{\ignorespaces  One frozen TETHER\ checkpoint, seed $0$, across five estimators and three arenas; every EPE and Bad1 cell is raw$\rightarrow $TETHER, lower is better. Two estimators were excluded from temporal-head training, so the lower-right block is the joint shift usually left unmeasured. DTCE is the macro reduction in temporal change error at lag $k{=}4$, higher is better; on development it is backbone-dependent and given in Sec.~\ref {sec:horizon} rather than here. Cells are pooled per backbone; prose figures that average per backbone--sequence cell will not reproduce from this table, and the DRENDS Bad3 of the abstract is not tabulated. \B  {T3.2} }}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:grid}{{I}{5}{}{}{}}
